    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Effective date: <strong>October 18, 2025</strong></p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Quick Amazon Importer</strong> ("we", "us", or "the App") collects, uses, and shares data when you install or use the Quick Amazon Importer Shopify app. By installing or using the App you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.</p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>When you install and use Quick Amazon Importer, we may collect the following categories of information:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Shop and account information:</strong> your Shopify shop domain, shop name, store email address, and the Shopify admin account ID that installed the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Access tokens & permissions:</strong> the OAuth access token and permissions needed to read and write products, product variants, images, and orders if you grant those permissions. We store the access token securely so the app can perform import and synchronization tasks on your behalf.</li>
      <li><strong>Product data:</strong> product titles, descriptions, SKUs, prices, inventory levels, images, ASINs and other Amazon identifiers, categories, and metafields that are imported or created by the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage and diagnostics:</strong> anonymized usage data, error logs, and performance metrics to help us maintain and improve the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Support communications:</strong> any messages you send to us (for example, support requests or feedback).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Provide the app features:</strong> to import product listings from Amazon, create or update products in your store, and keep imported data in sync.</li>
      <li><strong>Authentication & security:</strong> to authenticate API requests to your store and to protect your data.</li>
      <li><strong>Support & troubleshooting:</strong> to respond to your questions and fix bugs.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics & improvements:</strong> to analyze app usage, monitor performance, and improve the app features and reliability.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> to comply with legal obligations, enforce our terms, and protect rights and property.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Sharing & Third Parties</h2>
    <p>We will not sell your personal information. We may share data in the following situations:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> we use third-party service providers to host our servers, process payments (if applicable), send emails, and provide analytics and error-tracking. These providers only have access to the information necessary to perform their services and are contractually required to protect that data.</li>
      <li><strong>Amazon and related APIs:</strong> the App interacts with Amazon public/product resources to retrieve product information. When you use import features, the App may query Amazon endpoints to fetch product details using ASINs or public product pages.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal requests:</strong> we may disclose information to comply with laws, legal processes, or to protect our rights and safety.</li>
      <li><strong>Business transfers:</strong> if the App or its assets are sold, merged, or transferred, user data may be transferred as part of that transaction.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain your store information, product imports, and related data for as long as your account exists or as needed to provide the services. If you uninstall the app, we will stop performing syncs; we may retain backups or aggregated information for a reasonable period to comply with legal obligations or to prevent fraud. If you want your data deleted sooner, see the "Your Rights" section below.</p>

    <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights regarding your personal data, such as the right to access, correct, or delete your personal data, the right to object to processing, and the right to data portability. To exercise these rights, contact us at the address below. We will respond in accordance with applicable law.</p>

    <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect data against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. These measures include encrypted storage for sensitive credentials, access controls, and periodic security reviews. However, no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed to be 100% secure.</p>

    <h2>7. Children</h2>
    <p>The App is not intended for use by children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe we have collected information from a child, please contact us and we will take steps to remove that information.</p>

    <h2>8. International Transfers</h2>
    <p>If you are located outside of the country where our servers operate, your data may be transferred to and processed in other countries. By using the App, you consent to these transfers where permitted by law.</p>

    <h2>9. How to Uninstall or Delete Data</h2>
    <p>To remove the App from your store, uninstall it via your Shopify admin. Uninstalling the App stops further access to your store data. If you would like us to remove data we have stored for your shop (for example, imported products or logs), please contact us and we will assist with deletion requests.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have questions, requests, or complaints about this Privacy Policy, or if you wish to exercise your rights, contact us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Developer / Company:</strong> Quick Amazon Importer</li>
      <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@quick-amazon-importer.example">support@quick-amazon-importer.example</a> (replace with your support email)</li>
      <li><strong>Address:</strong> (Optional) Your company address</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. Changes to this Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy occasionally. If we make material changes, we will post the updated policy with a new effective date. Your continued use of the App after changes indicates acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

    <footer>
      <p>Quick Amazon Importer is an independent application created to help Shopify merchants import product listings from Amazon for use in their Shopify stores. This privacy policy applies only to data collected by the Quick Amazon Importer app and not to third-party sites linked from the app.</p>
